{"id": "EUVD-2026-59027", "enisaUuid": "9abbeb53-bcc4-3b04-8ba4-0ff3b9d03792", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlocking/rt: Fix the incorrect RCU protection in rt_spin_unlock()\n\nrt_spin_unlock() releases the RCU protection before unlocking the\nlock. That opens the door for the following UAF scenario:\n\n T1\t\t\t\t\tT2\n spin_lock(&p->lock);\t\trcu_read_lock();\n invalidate(p);\t\t\tp = rcu_dereference(ptr);\n rcu_assign_pointer(ptr, NULL);\tif (!p) return;\n spin_unlock(&p->lock);\t\tspin_lock(&p->lock)\n \t\t\t\t   lock(&lock->lock);\n\t\t\t\t   rcu_read_lock();\n kfree_rcu(p);\t\t\trcu_read_unlock();\n\t\t\t\t....\n\t\t\t\tspin_unlock(&p->lock)\n\t\t\t\t  rcu_read_unlock(); // Ends grace period\n rcu_do_batch()\n   kfree(p);\n\t\t\t    UAF ->\t  rt_mutex_cmpxchg_release(&lock->lock...)\n\nRegular spinlocks keep preemption disabled accross the unlock operation,\nwhich provides full RCU protection, but the RT substitution fails to\nresemble that. Same applies for the rwlock substitution.\n\nMove the rcu_read_unlock() invocation past the unlock operations to match\nthe non-RT semantics. This makes it asymmetric vs. rt_xxx_lock(), but\nthat's harmless as the caller needs to hold RCU read lock across the lock\noperation. The migrate_enable() call stays before the unlock operation\nbecause there is no per CPU operation in the unlock path which would\nrequire migration to be kept disabled.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:52:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:19:26", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af28d801cd2db4cc7378554499bd4a5d84a5517e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d1fcd64ab81200e02b7a6db5eb1da8e244e8289", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3cfaac77b3c32ac3940df28866de263c3f45d24c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f0d56d3f1e88f20f6e46109402f8c15d59bac37", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/633cadbc0b8323f5cc140a285d2432089dbb534e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83f9fb561c1c3917e19f95523dd933c7d30291aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89038cc87d80c77e7aa6f42a64b2573b74af339f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72069", "GHSA-mgq9-4f63-hxm9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.73, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0da0e321-3992-3935-bc97-a2e938fc2527", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f383b6dc96e976dfbf2721b0bf10bd96103b341 <83f9fb561c1c3917e19f95523dd933c7d30291aa"}, {"id": "32cbd2a3-6b2f-3221-97ef-c3546bc5588d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}, {"id": "4f456c99-9e66-3147-84f9-5db41449c778", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "5ab566b4-7a84-3b33-ae7a-39452dca84df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f383b6dc96e976dfbf2721b0bf10bd96103b341 <633cadbc0b8323f5cc140a285d2432089dbb534e"}, {"id": "61387a65-e395-3a49-bad4-530af3e46321", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.184"}, {"id": "81664b69-3a30-303e-987f-8cb4b55fbcf1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f383b6dc96e976dfbf2721b0bf10bd96103b341 <3cfaac77b3c32ac3940df28866de263c3f45d24c"}, {"id": "863754ad-a358-34b7-88f2-a77697c2778b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "8d32b158-6842-3f48-99a2-d80f74630a8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.217"}, {"id": "8e1513fe-9079-336d-862f-6c92d8ca91d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "998560fb-624c-38c4-a7d0-0e8c0fbaec66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f383b6dc96e976dfbf2721b0bf10bd96103b341 <1f0d56d3f1e88f20f6e46109402f